# ── Secrets — never commit ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These were tracked and pushed to two PUBLIC GitHub repos. The .dat files are
# not protection: _get_secret() returns a constant that lives in this same
# repository, so anyone who can read the code can decrypt them.
service_account.json
oauth_client.json
**/service_account.json
**/*service_account*.json
**/firebase*.json
config/*.dat
*.pem
*.p12
.env
.env.*
generate_oauth_token.py
encrypt_backup_creds.py

# Scratch database dumps left by debugging (hundreds of MB)
_chk_*.db
_check_*.db
*.db.gz

# Runtime artefacts of ONE shop, never product files. catalog.json is rebuilt
# from the store's own database every time web purchase is opened; launcher.html
# was a stale 857 KB copy carrying 12 GSTINs and 19 drug licence numbers of real
# suppliers, referenced by nothing. Both were being bundled into the EXE and
# copied over every shop's own catalog on launch.
web_app/catalog.json
web_app/launcher.html

# ── Kept out of git (2026-09-19): secrets, this PC's state, build output ──
# Firebase admin SDK keys - not matched by the *service_account* patterns above
**/*adminsdk*.json
# config/ holds this machine's runtime state (install id, printer settings,
# queued sync data for stores, logs). Build profiles are source.
config/*
!config/build_profile_*.txt
